":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative accuracy under any weight spread. O(n³) time, n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kemenyconstant()"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Kemeny constant: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transition rates, a loop taken with probability 2w\/d(v)) from a vertex to a target drawn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the stationary distribution, which does not depend on the start; Σ_{i≥2} 1\/μᵢ over the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"normalized Laplacian spectrum. nil when the graph is not connected, 0 for zero or one vertex."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"extension"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","title":"Graph"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/kemenyConstant()":{"title":"kemenyConstant()","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProto